    "reason": "MIMIC-III demo is small, lab-defined only, underpowered for all action-target reference gates, and model wins are sparse point estimates."
  },
  "interpretation": [
    "The adapter successfully maps MIMIC-III demo labs, ICU vitals, urine output, and INPUTEVENTS_CV/MV treatments into the same observed-treatment 6h DKA proxy schema used by MIMIC-IV/eICU evaluators.",
    "The demo contains 42 lab-defined DKA-like stays before evaluable filtering and 40 evaluable stays, but 0 ICD-confirmed DKA stays in the local demo files.",
    "Action grids, treatment lifecycle grids, and pre-anchor history are present, but action-target support remains below the prior reference gates for fluids-to-MAP, insulin-to-glucose, and KCl-to-potassium.",
    "V5 only beats persistence for all-window MAP and active-DKA bicarbonate as point estimates; the presentation-only candidate only has small active-DKA point-estimate wins for pH, potassium, and sodium.",
    "This is useful as a third cross-dataset schema/robustness smoke test, not as evidence for checkpoint promotion or treatment-effect inference."
  ],
